            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 66-year-old male patient, admitted on 11/05/2008 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency, chest X-ray excluding pneumonia or pneumothorax, and pulse oximetry monitoring throughout the stay. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 12/05/2008 in stable condition. Pulmonary rehabilitation and optimisation of inhaler technique were recommended. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
